  "worked_solution": "We notice that $E$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix and $F$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $F$ and $4$ rows in $E.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ equals the number of rows in $E,$ the matrices $F$ and $E$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $FE$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{F}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{E}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={FE}_{2\\times 2}\n$$",
